- action(n1, "start production process"): Hallucinates an extra initial step; the source text describes a single starting activity ("initiate production according to the instructions and terms specified in the work order and contract"), which is already captured by action(n2,...).
- action(n6, "end process"): Introduces an unwarranted intermediate action before termination; the description simply states "Finally, the process concludes", implying a direct transition from action(n5,...) to end(e1).
- action(n2, "initiate production according to work order and contract"): Payload omits explicit source qualifiers ("according to the instructions and terms specified in..."), violating SMC2 faithfulness.
- precedence(n1, n2) & precedence(n5, n6): Insert artificial control-flow hops that distort the exact sequential progression outlined in the text, violating SMC3.